      ],
      "tier": "city",
      "region": "The Salt Hills",
      "identity": "The border garrison. The most 'normal'-looking place in Argonia, which makes it the strangest by contrast. Industry: the border - customs, the Legion, and the ugly living memory of Dunmer slave-raids coming down the passes. Tension: the Legion is under-funded and outnumbered eight to one by the people it polices, and everyone has done the arithmetic. Layout tells you: Imperial grid inside the walls, Argonian sprawl leaning against the OUTSIDE of them - two towns sharing one wall from opposite sides.",
