      "x": 1905.5,
      "z": 4450.0,
      "source_px": [
        988,
        1260
      ],
      "tier": "town",
      "region": "Western Rootlands",
      "identity": "A town that exists to feed and guard a prison. The Imperial-built Blackrose Prison squats over it and the town is its outbuildings. Industry: incarceration. Tension: half the townsfolk are ex-guards and half are inmates' families, and the warden is not who the Empire thinks he is. Layout tells you: there is no square - only corridors between compound walls. Every street is a checkpoint.",
